/* Deep aspect interpretations, part 2: pairs led by Mars through Lilith */
window.AstroDeep = window.AstroDeep || {};
window.AstroDeep.aspects2 = {
  "mars|jupiter": {
    theme: "Mars wants to act now; Jupiter wants the action to mean something and to be bigger. Together they negotiate how much drive, risk and confidence you bring to what you go after, and when enough is enough.",
    fusion: "With Mars conjunct Jupiter, your drive comes with built-in optimism. You tend to start things with enthusiasm and genuine courage, and you often rally others simply by believing the goal is possible. Sport, travel, entrepreneurial projects and causes suit you. The shadow is overreach: taking on three commitments where one would do, or pushing past a sensible limit because stopping feels like losing.",
    flow: "Effort and luck seem to cooperate for you. When you commit to something, you usually find the stamina and the timing, and people back you because your confidence feels earned. You recover quickly from setbacks and rarely stay flat for long. Because it comes so easily, you may coast on energy instead of building skill, and wonder later why a more disciplined peer went further.",
    tension: "Part of you wants to charge ahead, and part of you keeps raising the stakes until the plan becomes unmanageable. This can look like overcommitting, arguing on principle, or impatience with anyone who seems to think small. In relationships you may push your views too hard. Integration comes when you pick fewer battles, pace your enthusiasm, and let conviction be backed by steady follow-through."
  },
  "mars|saturn": {
    theme: "The accelerator meets the brake. Mars wants to move and assert; Saturn asks for patience, structure and proof. The negotiation is between impulse and discipline, and how safe it feels to use your strength.",
    fusion: "Mars conjunct Saturn gives controlled, sustained force. You tend to work steadily at hard things long after others have quit, and your anger usually runs cold and focused. Early on, you may have learned that asserting yourself had consequences, so you held back. Over time this becomes real mastery: the builder, the endurance athlete, the person who finishes what they start.",
    flow: "You have a practical gift for pacing effort. You know how to break a big task into stages, and you rarely waste energy on drama or false starts. Employers and teams trust you with responsibility because you deliver, often quietly and on time. The risk is that caution becomes a habit, and you stop taking the bold swing your skill has already earned you.",
    tension: "You may feel stuck between wanting to act and a deep sense that you are not allowed to, or that it will go wrong. Frustration can build up and release as sharp irritability, or it turns inward as fatigue and self-criticism. With bosses and authority figures there can be friction. Integration looks like steady, chosen effort: small consistent actions that prove your drive is safe to use."
  },
  "mars|uranus": {
    theme: "Drive meets the urge to break free. Mars wants to act; Uranus wants to act differently, suddenly and on its own terms. You negotiate between courage and recklessness, independence and cooperation.",
    fusion: "Mars conjunct Uranus runs on a fast, electric current. You tend to act on instinct, make sudden decisions, and bristle at being told what to do. Innovation, activism, technology and anything that needs quick reflexes can suit you well. The same charge can produce accidents, abrupt exits from jobs or relationships, and a gnawing restlessness whenever life settles into routine.",
    flow: "You adapt quickly and respond well in a crisis. When something breaks, you are often the first to try an unexpected fix, and you enjoy doing things your own way. Others tend to find your independence refreshing and a little contagious. Left unchecked, the ease can make you impatient with slower, steadier work that would give your ideas a lasting shape.",
    tension: "There is a restless push against restriction, and it can flare without warning. You might quit on impulse, pick fights with rules that feel arbitrary, or feel caged in close relationships. Others can experience you as unpredictable. Integration involves finding outlets for that voltage, such as physical challenge or genuine reform work, and learning to pause for one breath before you break something you value."
  },
  "mars|neptune": {
    theme: "Assertion meets dissolution. Mars wants a clear target; Neptune blurs edges and seeks meaning, compassion or escape. The negotiation is about acting on ideals without losing your direction or your energy.",
    fusion: "When Mars and Neptune are conjunct, your drive tends to be fuelled by imagination, empathy or a sense of calling. You may act most readily on behalf of others, or work best in art, music, dance, healing or spiritual service. Direct confrontation can feel uncomfortable, so anger may come out sideways. Energy levels can fluctuate, and you usually work best when genuinely inspired.",
    flow: "You have a graceful, intuitive way of acting. You often sense the right move without being able to explain it, and your efforts carry a quality of care or artistry. Movement, performance and compassionate work tend to come naturally. The risk is drifting, letting inspiration carry you while skipping the practical steps that turn a vision into something real and finished.",
    tension: "You may struggle to know what you actually want, or to defend it once you do. This can show up as passive resistance, avoidance, or a pattern of fighting hard for others while neglecting yourself. Sometimes energy drains away for no clear reason. Integration involves naming your desires plainly, setting clean boundaries, and directing your idealism into concrete, finishable acts."
  },
  "mars|pluto": {
    theme: "Two planets of force and will. Mars acts; Pluto wants control, depth and transformation. You negotiate between raw intensity and the power to use it wisely, without dominating or being dominated.",
    fusion: "Mars conjunct Pluto gives extraordinary willpower. When you commit, you tend to go all the way, and you can endure pressure that breaks others. This suits crisis work, research, surgery, recovery and any field that needs relentless focus. Anger can be volcanic, so learning how and when to release it matters. Used well, this is the energy that rebuilds from the ground up.",
    flow: "You have deep reserves of stamina and a strategic mind. You tend to see where the real power lies in a situation and act on it quietly and effectively. You can regenerate after exhaustion or loss. Because your intensity feels normal to you, you may underestimate how strong it looks to others, or rely on sheer force when finesse would serve better.",
    tension: "Power struggles are a recurring theme. You may meet control with fierce resistance, or find yourself trying to control outcomes and people. Anger can be held in for a long time, then erupt. Relationships may feel like tests of will, with neither person willing to yield. Integration comes when you channel that intensity into a clear purpose, and use your strength to protect, heal and rebuild."
  },
  "mars|chiron": {
    theme: "Action meets the wound. Mars wants to assert and compete; Chiron carries a place of hurt and hard-won wisdom. You negotiate how to act with courage when assertion itself has been painful.",
    fusion: "Mars conjunct Chiron often points to an early wound around anger, confidence, the body or being allowed to fight for yourself. You may alternate between holding back and overcompensating. Over time this becomes a particular gift: you can champion others who have been silenced, coach people through physical or emotional setbacks, and model a courage that includes vulnerability.",
    flow: "You tend to have a natural instinct for helping others find their strength. Coaching, physiotherapy, advocacy and mentoring can suit you well, because you understand the fear behind hesitation. Your own healing tends to move through action, such as movement or taking a stand. The risk is focusing so much on other people's courage that you skip over your own unfinished hurts.",
    tension: "Asserting yourself may feel risky, as though every confrontation reopens an old sore. You might swing between avoiding conflict and reacting harder than a situation calls for. Injuries or burnout can come from pushing through pain. Integration involves treating your anger as information, acting from self-respect instead of defensiveness, and letting your scars inform how you stand up for others."
  },
  "mars|northNode": {
    theme: "Drive meets direction. Mars supplies energy and courage; the North Node points to the growth your life keeps inviting. The negotiation is whether your drive is serving that growth or running on old habits.",
    fusion: "With Mars on the North Node, courage is part of your path. You tend to grow by acting, taking initiative and learning to compete or lead, even when it feels uncomfortable. Situations that demand boldness keep appearing until you rise to them. The challenge is to direct that fire towards your real purpose, since scattered effort tends to leave you feeling oddly unfulfilled.",
    flow: "Your drive tends to support your development naturally. When you take action in the direction of growth, doors open, and effort feels meaningful instead of draining. You may find that sport, physical work or bold decisions have shaped your life in positive ways. Because the energy flows easily, you might not notice when you are coasting and could be stretching much further.",
    tension: "Your instinct to act may pull against the direction you are growing in. Sometimes you fight the wrong battles, or push hard in familiar ways while the real development asks for something else. At other times growth demands a courage you hesitate to find. Integration means asking where your energy is actually going and redirecting it towards what genuinely moves your life forward."
  },
  "mars|lilith": {
    theme: "Assertion meets the untamed. Mars wants to act and claim; Lilith holds the raw, exiled parts of desire and anger. You negotiate how to express your instincts without shame or destructive rebellion.",
    fusion: "Mars conjunct Lilith gives fierce, unapologetic energy, especially around sexuality, anger and autonomy. You may have been told early on that your strength was too much. Today you tend to refuse to be tamed, and you can be magnetic and confronting in equal measure. The work is to own that power consciously, so it fuels your life instead of burning bridges.",
    flow: "You have an easy relationship with your own instincts. You tend to know what you desire and act on it without much guilt, and this confidence can be liberating for the people around you. You may be drawn to challenging taboos or defending the marginalised. The risk is assuming everyone shares your comfort, and missing the moments when your directness genuinely wounds.",
    tension: "There can be a pull between desire and the fear of what happens if you show it. Suppressed anger or sexuality may leak out in unexpected ways, through provocation, sudden rebellion, or relationships that become battlegrounds. You may feel punished for being too much. Integration comes from giving your raw energy honest, deliberate outlets and refusing to apologise for having needs."
  },
  "mars|asc": {
    theme: "Drive meets presence. Mars is how you assert; the Ascendant is how you meet the world and are first seen. You negotiate how directly your energy shows and how others read your assertiveness.",
    fusion: "Mars conjunct the Ascendant makes your energy visible from the first moment. You tend to come across as direct, active and quick to respond, and people often see you as brave or competitive. Physical activity usually matters a great deal to your wellbeing. The shadow is coming on too strong, or reacting before you have read the room, which others may take as aggression.",
    flow: "You carry your energy with ease. People often experience you as capable, lively and ready to take the lead, and you tend to start things confidently. Your body and your will seem to work together without much friction. Because this comes naturally, you may not notice when you dominate a group, or rely on first impressions when a slower approach would build more trust.",
    tension: "Your way of asserting yourself can clash with how you want to be seen, or with the people closest to you. With the opposition, partners may seem to carry the anger or competitiveness you keep hidden. With the square, you might swing between holding back and blurting things out. Integration involves owning your drive openly and learning to calibrate its volume to the situation."
  },
  "mars|mc": {
    theme: "Drive meets vocation. Mars is your will to act and compete; the Midheaven is your public role and direction. You negotiate how ambition, initiative and conflict play out in your career and reputation.",
    fusion: "Mars conjunct the Midheaven brings strong career drive. You tend to want to lead, pioneer or win in your field, and you may be known for your energy, courage or competitiveness. Work involving action, engineering, sport, emergency services or starting a business can suit you. You may clash with bosses until you are running things yourself, which is often where you do best.",
    flow: "Your initiative tends to support your career naturally. You take opportunities when they appear, handle pressure well, and others recognise your capacity to get things done. Leadership may come to you without much fuss. The risk is relying on drive alone, and neglecting the relationships and patience that would take your work from merely busy to truly influential.",
    tension: "Ambition and conflict can tangle around your career. You might clash with authority, feel frustrated by slow progress, or feel pulled between work goals and your private life. Sometimes tension at home spills into work, or the reverse. Integration comes when you choose your professional battles, direct competitive energy towards meaningful goals, and build a path where your drive has room."
  },
  "jupiter|saturn": {
    theme: "Expansion meets limitation. Jupiter says yes, grow, believe; Saturn says wait, test, build properly. The negotiation is between faith and realism, and between opportunity and responsibility in how you grow.",
    fusion: "Jupiter conjunct Saturn marks the start of a roughly twenty-year social cycle, so you share it with others born around the same time. Personally, it tends to give a sober kind of ambition. You want to grow, but in a structured way, and you often achieve steady success through long-term plans. The challenge is letting yourself hope without first demanding a guarantee.",
    flow: "You have a good instinct for balancing risk and caution. You tend to spot realistic opportunities, make plans that actually work, and grow your life in sustainable steps. Management, law, teaching and business often suit you. The ease can make you content with moderate success, so you may never test how much further a bolder move could take you.",
    tension: "You may swing between optimism and doubt, starting with enthusiasm and then stalling, or feeling that every opportunity comes with a heavy price. There can be friction between your beliefs and your sense of duty. Integration involves letting each check the other: dreaming big, then building carefully, and trusting that faith and disciplined effort can pull in the same direction."
  },
  "jupiter|uranus": {
    theme: "Growth meets sudden change. Jupiter expands; Uranus liberates and disrupts. Together they negotiate how much freedom, experiment and unexpected opportunity you can welcome without scattering your life.",
    fusion: "Jupiter conjunct Uranus happens about every fourteen years, so it is shared with peers, but it often shows personally as a hunger for freedom and new ideas. You may experience sudden breaks and lucky turns, and you tend to be drawn to innovation, travel, technology or unconventional beliefs. Restlessness is the cost, especially when life settles into routine.",
    flow: "You tend to be open to new ideas and to find opportunity in change. When something unexpected happens, you often land on your feet, and you can spot trends before others do. Your enthusiasm for progress inspires people. The risk is chasing novelty and leaving projects unfinished once the excitement fades, or trusting luck where some planning would help.",
    tension: "You may feel torn between growth through stability and growth through breaking away. This can show as sudden changes of direction, rebellion against belief systems, or overconfidence in risky schemes. In relationships you may need more space than partners expect. Integration comes when you give your freedom a purpose, commit to a few chosen experiments, and see them through."
  },
  "jupiter|neptune": {
    theme: "Faith meets imagination. Jupiter seeks meaning and expansion; Neptune dissolves boundaries and longs for the ideal. The negotiation is between inspiring vision and the discernment to keep your feet on the ground.",
    fusion: "This conjunction happens about every thirteen years and colours the spiritual mood of those born under it. Personally, it tends to give a large heart and a vivid imagination. You may be drawn to spirituality, art, music, charity or healing, and you often see the best in people. The risk is idealising too much, or being generous past the point of wisdom.",
    flow: "You have a natural compassion and a gift for inspiring others. Creative, spiritual or humanitarian work tends to flow, and people often feel uplifted around you. You may have a strong intuitive sense of meaning. Because belief comes so easily, you might overlook practical details, or trust people and schemes without checking whether they deserve it.",
    tension: "Your ideals and your sense of reality may pull in different directions. This can show as disappointment when people fall short, overcommitment to causes, or escapism when life feels harsh. Boundaries around money, time or help can blur. Integration involves grounding your faith in daily practice, checking facts before you commit, and keeping compassion for yourself as well as others."
  },
  "jupiter|pluto": {
    theme: "Expansion meets depth and power. Jupiter enlarges whatever it touches; Pluto seeks control and transformation. You negotiate how to use ambition and influence without becoming consumed by them.",
    fusion: "Jupiter conjunct Pluto occurs roughly every thirteen years, marking a peer group with big ambitions around power and change. Personally, it can give formidable drive to make an impact. You tend to think in terms of large-scale influence, whether in business, politics, research or healing. The shadow is obsession with success, or believing your cause justifies any means.",
    flow: "You have a quiet talent for building influence and seeing the bigger picture. You tend to recognise opportunities hidden beneath the surface and use resources strategically. Others often turn to you in a crisis because you can see what needs to change. The risk is growing complacent about your power, and not noticing when you have more influence than you realise.",
    tension: "Ambition can become a struggle with authority, ideology or yourself. You may push too hard, clash with powerful people, or feel that you must win completely. Beliefs can harden into dogma. In close relationships you might test loyalty. Integration comes when you use your conviction to empower others, stay open to changing your mind, and treat influence as a responsibility."
  },
  "jupiter|chiron": {
    theme: "Faith meets the wound. Jupiter seeks meaning and growth; Chiron carries a sore place and the wisdom it produces. You negotiate how to find hope and purpose through what has hurt you.",
    fusion: "Jupiter conjunct Chiron often turns pain into teaching. You may have been wounded around belief, education or trust in life, and later find that exactly this makes you a gifted mentor, counsellor or guide. You tend to find meaning in healing. The risk is making your wound your whole identity, or preaching recovery before you have fully lived it yourself.",
    flow: "You have a natural gift for helping others find hope. People often come to you when they are struggling, and your perspective can be healing because it is honest about pain. Teaching, counselling and spiritual work tend to suit you. Because it comes easily, you might skip over your own hurt and treat helping others as a substitute for doing your own work.",
    tension: "Your hopes and your wounds may seem at odds. You may swing between overconfidence and feeling fundamentally not enough, or lose faith when life does not go to plan. Sometimes you reach for grand answers to avoid feeling small, ordinary losses. Integration involves letting pain humble your beliefs, and letting those beliefs give your pain a sense of meaning."
  },
  "jupiter|northNode": {
    theme: "Growth meets destiny. Jupiter expands and brings opportunity; the North Node shows the direction of your development. You negotiate whether your optimism supports that growth or keeps you in comfortable territory.",
    fusion: "Jupiter on the North Node tends to bring generous support for growth. Opportunities, teachers and resources often appear when you move towards your purpose, and you usually grow through learning, travel or broadening your beliefs. The key is choosing the direction wisely, since Jupiter can make almost anything look promising. Faith in your path tends to be rewarded.",
    flow: "Your natural optimism and your life direction work well together. When you pursue growth, you tend to find encouragement, and people want to help. You may have an intuitive sense of where meaning lies. The risk is assuming everything will work out without effort, and letting good fortune replace the harder choices that would develop you further.",
    tension: "What looks like a good opportunity may pull you away from your real growth. You might say yes to too much, or pursue expansion that feels exciting yet leaves you unfulfilled. Inherited beliefs may clash with your path. Integration involves being selective, checking whether an opportunity serves your development, and letting some attractive offers pass without regret."
  },
  "jupiter|lilith": {
    theme: "Expansion meets the exiled. Jupiter enlarges and blesses; Lilith holds the raw, rejected parts of you. You negotiate how to give your untamed side room, meaning and dignity.",
    fusion: "Jupiter conjunct Lilith tends to magnify your wild side. You may have strong convictions about freedom, sexuality or rejecting convention, and you might become an outspoken voice for what others hide. Your appetite for life is big and unashamed. The risk is excess, or turning rebellion into a belief system that leaves little room for nuance or doubt.",
    flow: "You have an easy, generous relationship with your own shadow. You tend to accept the parts of yourself others might hide, and this acceptance extends to other people. Your openness about desire or difference can be healing for those around you. The ease can make you careless with boundaries, or lead you to assume everyone is as unbothered by taboo as you are.",
    tension: "Your beliefs and your raw instincts may be at odds. You might hold values that shame your desires, or rebel against belief systems in ways that cost you. This can show as swings between moral righteousness and indulgence. Integration comes when you build a personal philosophy wide enough to include your instincts, allowing both freedom and meaning."
  },
  "jupiter|asc": {
    theme: "Expansion meets presence. Jupiter brings warmth, confidence and appetite; the Ascendant is how you show up and are first seen. The negotiation is how much of that largeness you carry into the room.",
    fusion: "Jupiter conjunct the Ascendant often gives a warm, generous presence. People tend to find you encouraging and easy to trust, and you may seem luckier or more confident than you feel. You often have a strong appetite for life, travel and learning. The shadow is excess, whether in promises, food, spending or simply taking up more space than a moment needs.",
    flow: "Your natural manner invites goodwill. You tend to make friends easily and people want to help you, which smooths many situations. You often bring optimism into groups that need it. Because this generosity comes so easily, you may overpromise, or rely on charm when a situation needs more careful attention or patient follow-through.",
    tension: "You may feel pulled between expanding and presenting a controlled image, or partners may seem to hold the confidence you lack. With the square, overconfidence can alternate with self-doubt, and you might overreach socially. Integration involves letting your warmth be real and grounded, and making sure your enthusiasm matches what you can actually deliver."
  },
  "jupiter|mc": {
    theme: "Growth meets vocation. Jupiter expands whatever it touches; the Midheaven is your career and public standing. You negotiate how big you aim professionally and what your work means to you.",
    fusion: "Jupiter conjunct the Midheaven often signals professional growth and recognition. You tend to want work that means something, and fields such as teaching, law, publishing, travel or leadership can suit you. Opportunities often come through reputation and goodwill. The risk is taking on too much, or assuming success will continue without the discipline that built it.",
    flow: "Your career tends to benefit from optimism and good timing. People in authority often support you, and you have a way of finding roles that feel meaningful. Your enthusiasm for your field can inspire colleagues. The ease may make you settle for comfortable success, or avoid the harder moves that would take your work to a new level.",
    tension: "Ambition and meaning may pull against each other. You might chase prestige that feels empty, or feel torn between career expansion and home or family. Overpromising at work can become a pattern. Integration involves choosing goals that match your values, balancing public growth with private needs, and backing big visions with realistic, staged plans."
  },
  "saturn|uranus": {
    theme: "Structure meets revolution. Saturn preserves and builds; Uranus disrupts and liberates. The negotiation is between the old and the new, tradition and progress, and the safety of rules versus the pull of freedom.",
    fusion: "This conjunction is generational, shared by everyone born over a year or so, and it marks a collective effort to rebuild outdated structures. It becomes personal when it touches your Sun, Moon or an angle. Then you tend to be a practical reformer, someone who changes systems from within and gives new ideas a form that can actually last.",
    flow: "Across your generation this aspect supports steady, useful change. When it links to your Sun, Moon or angles, it can give you a talent for combining innovation with realism. You tend to update old methods without throwing out what still works. The risk is complacency: being comfortable enough with gradual change that you avoid a break that is genuinely overdue.",
    tension: "Generationally, this reflects friction between tradition and progress. When it contacts your personal planets or angles, you may swing between wanting security and needing freedom, or feel caught between duty and rebellion. You might resist change for years, then break away suddenly. Integration involves honouring both needs by building a solid base that still leaves room for reinvention."
  },
  "saturn|neptune": {
    theme: "Reality meets the dream. Saturn defines, limits and makes things concrete; Neptune dissolves, imagines and longs. You negotiate between discipline and inspiration, and between fear and faith.",
    fusion: "Saturn conjunct Neptune is generational, occurring every thirty-six years or so, and reflects a collective effort to give ideals a practical form. It becomes personal when it touches your Sun, Moon, Ascendant or Midheaven. Then you may have a knack for building dreams: organising spiritual work, running creative projects, or structuring care. Disillusionment can be an important teacher for you.",
    flow: "Generationally this supports grounded idealism. When it links with your key personal points, you tend to have a gift for making the intangible real, in art, film, design, healing or charity. You may combine intuition with a steady sense of structure. The risk is under-using it, treating your practical imagination as a hobby when it could be a real contribution.",
    tension: "For a generation this reflects the gap between ideals and reality. When it connects to your personal points, you may feel torn between hard facts and hope, or struggle with vague anxieties that are hard to name. Boundaries can feel either too rigid or too loose. Integration comes when you give your dreams a schedule, and allow faith to soften your fears."
  },
  "saturn|pluto": {
    theme: "Structure meets transformation. Saturn builds and endures; Pluto tears down and regenerates. The negotiation is about power, control and resilience, and deciding what should be preserved and what must end.",
    fusion: "Saturn conjunct Pluto is generational, happening roughly every thirty-three to thirty-eight years, and marks a collective confrontation with power and its limits. It becomes personal when it touches your Sun, Moon or angles. Then you tend to have immense endurance and a serious, focused will. You may be drawn to rebuilding institutions, or to work that deals directly with crisis.",
    flow: "Across your generation this aspect supports resilience under pressure. If it touches your key personal points, you tend to have a talent for sustained, strategic effort and for rebuilding after loss. You are often the calm one in a crisis, quietly working out what needs to happen next. The risk is taking your toughness for granted, and never admitting when you need rest or support.",
    tension: "Generationally, this reflects struggle with authority and systems of control. When it contacts your personal planets or angles, you may feel pressure to be strong at all costs, or experience power struggles with institutions or bosses. Fear of losing control can harden into rigidity. Integration involves accepting endings, using your strength with integrity, and letting some control go."
  },
  "saturn|chiron": {
    theme: "Structure meets the wound. Saturn tests and builds; Chiron carries hurt and healing. You negotiate how responsibility, limits and time can turn a painful place into genuine authority.",
    fusion: "Saturn conjunct Chiron often indicates a wound around authority, achievement or feeling good enough. You may have been judged harshly early on, or carried responsibility before you were ready. With time this aspect tends to mature into real wisdom. You can become a patient teacher or mentor, especially for people who believe they have already failed.",
    flow: "You have a natural capacity to learn from difficulty and turn it into structure. You tend to heal through discipline, routine and gradual effort, and you can help others build practical recovery plans. People see you as trustworthy in hard times. The ease may lead you to intellectualise pain, managing it neatly on paper while avoiding actually feeling it.",
    tension: "You may be hard on yourself, as though your wound proves some basic lack. Fear of failure can hold you back, or you might overcompensate by working relentlessly. Authority figures may trigger old hurt. Integration comes from building a gentler discipline, recognising that your limits are part of your expertise, and letting time do some of the healing."
  },
  "saturn|northNode": {
    theme: "Structure meets destiny. Saturn asks for discipline, patience and maturity; the North Node shows the growth your life keeps inviting. You negotiate how commitment and responsibility support or restrict that development.",
    fusion: "Saturn on the North Node tends to make growth a serious, long-term project. You may feel a strong sense of duty around your path, and development often comes through responsibility, hard work and learning from setbacks. Progress can feel slow early on, then steady and solid. The challenge is making sure fear of failure never stops you stepping forward at all.",
    flow: "You tend to have a practical sense of how to build your future. Discipline and commitment support your growth naturally, and you often find mentors or structures that help at the right time. You are good at long-term planning. The risk is becoming so cautious or dutiful that you choose the safe version of your path and miss the more meaningful one.",
    tension: "Responsibilities may seem to pull against your growth. You might feel held back by duty, family expectations or fear, or push yourself into rigid structures that do not fit your direction. Frustration with slow progress is common. Integration involves choosing commitments that genuinely serve your development, and seeing that patience itself is part of the growth."
  },
  "saturn|lilith": {
    theme: "Control meets the untamed. Saturn sets rules, limits and consequences; Lilith holds your raw, rejected instincts. The negotiation is between the need for order and the need to be wholly yourself.",
    fusion: "Saturn conjunct Lilith often points to early experiences of shame or restriction around sexuality, anger or independence. You may have learned to control your wild side tightly. Over time this can become a disciplined kind of power: you know your instincts well and express them deliberately. The work is to release old fear and allow your nature more room.",
    flow: "You tend to have a mature relationship with your shadow. You can acknowledge difficult desires calmly and set sensible boundaries around them. Others may trust you with their secrets because you do not judge. The ease can become over-control, so you rarely let yourself be spontaneous or messy, even when it would be healthy and freeing.",
    tension: "Part of you may feel you have to hide or suppress your instincts to be acceptable. This can show as rigid self-control followed by sudden rebellion, or relationships where authority and desire clash. You might fear punishment simply for being yourself. Integration involves building rules that respect your instincts, and allowing yourself to be powerful without apology."
  },
  "saturn|asc": {
    theme: "Structure meets presence. Saturn brings reserve, responsibility and caution; the Ascendant shapes how you appear and approach life. You negotiate how serious, guarded or reliable you seem to others.",
    fusion: "Saturn conjunct the Ascendant tends to give a serious, composed presence. People may have seen you as mature, capable or reserved even when you were young. You often approach life cautiously and prefer to prove yourself before relaxing. With age this usually softens into grounded authority. The shadow is self-consciousness, or holding back warmth out of fear.",
    flow: "You come across as dependable, and people tend to trust you with responsibility. You manage first impressions carefully and often grow more confident with every decade. Your body and health may respond well to steady routines and discipline. The ease can make you too careful, so others experience you as distant when you are simply taking your time.",
    tension: "You may feel restricted in how you present yourself, or partners may seem to bring responsibility and limits into your life. With the square, self-doubt can clash with the need to seem in control, and you might feel constantly judged. Integration comes from gradually trusting yourself, letting others see your uncertainty, and allowing structure to support you instead of hiding you."
  },
  "saturn|mc": {
    theme: "Structure meets vocation. Saturn brings ambition, discipline and tests; the Midheaven is your career and public role. You negotiate how hard you work for recognition and what success costs you.",
    fusion: "Saturn conjunct the Midheaven often gives strong ambition and a serious attitude to career. You tend to build success slowly and earn it through persistence, and you may reach real authority in your field later in life. Pressure to achieve may have come early, perhaps from a parent. The shadow is fear of failure or public judgement, which can make you overly cautious.",
    flow: "You have a practical talent for building a career. You tend to understand hierarchies, meet responsibilities and earn trust over time, and your reputation often rests on quiet reliability. Senior people notice. The ease can make you satisfied with a secure role, so you might avoid the risk of moving towards a more meaningful vocation.",
    tension: "Career and personal life may compete, or you might feel blocked by authority figures. With the square, success can seem constantly delayed. You might overwork to prove yourself, or fear being exposed as not good enough. Integration involves defining success on your own terms, balancing duty with rest, and recognising that setbacks tend to strengthen your long-term standing."
  },
  "uranus|neptune": {
    theme: "Revolution meets imagination. Uranus seeks freedom and innovation; Neptune seeks transcendence and unity. As a generational pairing, it shapes how collective ideals and new technologies reshape shared dreams.",
    fusion: "Uranus conjunct Neptune is a rare generational aspect, occurring about every 170 years. Those born roughly between 1988 and 1996 share it, and as a group tend to blend technology with spirituality and imagination. It becomes personal when it touches your Sun, Moon or angles. Then you may feel called to create new visions through digital art, music or spiritual innovation.",
    flow: "Generationally, this aspect supports intuitive innovation and fresh ideals. When it links with your personal planets or angles, you tend to have a gift for sensing collective moods and translating them into creative or technological form. Your ideas can feel slightly ahead of their time. The risk is drifting on inspiration and never grounding it into something concrete.",
    tension: "For a generation this reflects friction between ideals and rapid change, and a restless search for meaning. When it contacts your personal points, you may swing between inspired breakthroughs and confusion, or struggle to know which vision to follow. Integration involves choosing one clear direction, testing ideas against reality, and still keeping space for intuition."
  },
  "uranus|pluto": {
    theme: "Revolution meets transformation. Uranus disrupts and liberates; Pluto destroys and regenerates. This generational pairing negotiates radical change: tearing down old systems and building new ones in their place.",
    fusion: "Uranus conjunct Pluto is generational; people born in the mid-1960s carry it, and it is associated with social upheaval and radical change. It becomes personal when it touches your Sun, Moon, Ascendant or Midheaven. Then you may feel driven to transform systems, challenge authority and pursue freedom intensely. Your life can involve sudden, far-reaching changes of direction.",
    flow: "Generationally, this aspect supports adaptation and reform. When it links to your personal points, you tend to handle upheaval well and see opportunity in crisis. You may have a talent for driving change with strategic insight, knowing where one push will shift a whole system. The risk is taking that resilience for granted and never examining what you are changing, or why.",
    tension: "For a generation this reflects conflict between freedom and control. When it contacts your personal planets or angles, you may feel restless under authority, or experience abrupt endings that force reinvention. Power struggles and rebellion can become recurring themes. Integration comes when you channel that intensity into purposeful reform, knowing which structures to break and which to rebuild."
  },
  "uranus|chiron": {
    theme: "Freedom meets the wound. Uranus seeks independence and change; Chiron carries hurt and healing. You negotiate how being different has hurt you, and how it might become your greatest gift.",
    fusion: "Uranus conjunct Chiron often indicates a wound around feeling different, excluded or out of step. You may have been the odd one out at school or in your family. Over time this tends to become a gift: you can offer unconventional healing, champion outsiders and find new ways of addressing old pain. Your own breakthroughs often arrive suddenly.",
    flow: "You tend to have a natural talent for original approaches to healing. You can see problems from fresh angles, and people who feel different often find you understanding and easy to talk to. Alternative therapies, technology or social reform may suit you. The ease can make you dismiss conventional wisdom too quickly, even when it could genuinely help.",
    tension: "You may feel torn between the need to belong and the need to be free, and old hurt can make you rebel or withdraw without warning. Feeling misunderstood may be familiar. Integration involves accepting your difference as a strength, allowing healing to happen gradually, and finding communities that value your originality without asking you to shrink it."
  },
  "uranus|northNode": {
    theme: "Innovation meets direction. Uranus brings sudden change and originality; the North Node shows the growth your life keeps inviting. You negotiate how much disruption and freedom your development actually needs.",
    fusion: "Uranus on the North Node tends to make change part of your path. You may grow through breaking with family tradition, experimenting, or following an unusual route that others struggle to understand. Sudden events often redirect you. The challenge is to choose change consciously, so that freedom supports your growth without turning into restlessness for its own sake.",
    flow: "Your originality tends to support your development. When you follow your unusual interests, opportunities appear, and you may find allies in communities, networks or online groups. You adapt easily to new circumstances. The risk is relying on novelty, or leaving situations just as they begin to stretch you in useful and lasting ways.",
    tension: "Your need for freedom may pull against the direction of your growth. You might walk away from situations that would have helped you, or feel knocked off course by unexpected disruptions. Integration involves asking honestly whether a change serves your development or helps you avoid it, and allowing some stability to become part of your growth."
  },
  "uranus|lilith": {
    theme: "Rebellion meets the untamed. Uranus seeks freedom and disruption; Lilith holds raw, exiled instincts. You negotiate how to express your wildness in ways that liberate instead of alienate.",
    fusion: "Uranus conjunct Lilith tends to give a fiercely independent streak, especially around sexuality, gender, anger or social norms. You may have little patience with convention, and you often challenge taboos in ways that inspire others to be more authentic. The risk is shock for its own sake, or rejecting closeness to protect your independence.",
    flow: "You have an easy relationship with your unconventional instincts. You tend to accept your own difference and express it with confidence, often freeing others to do the same. Activism or alternative communities may suit you. The ease can make you dismissive of people who need more time to accept change, including those who love you.",
    tension: "You may feel caught between the urge to rebel and a fear of rejection. This can show as sudden outbursts, abrupt breakups, or cycles of conforming and then rebelling. Integration involves owning your wild nature consistently, choosing deliberately when to challenge norms, and building connections strong enough to hold your independence."
  },
  "uranus|asc": {
    theme: "Originality meets presence. Uranus brings unpredictability, independence and innovation; the Ascendant shapes how you show up. You negotiate how unconventional you appear and how much stability you can tolerate.",
    fusion: "Uranus conjunct the Ascendant tends to give a distinctive, unconventional presence. People may see you as original, surprising or hard to categorise. You often need freedom in how you live and look, and you may change your appearance or direction suddenly. The shadow is restlessness, or keeping people at arm's length so nobody can pin you down.",
    flow: "You come across as refreshing and inventive. People tend to find your ideas stimulating, and you adapt quickly to new situations, jobs and places. Your originality can make you a quiet trendsetter. The ease may lead you to avoid commitments, or rely on novelty and first impressions instead of developing depth over time.",
    tension: "Your need for independence may clash with the people around you. With the opposition, partners may seem unpredictable, or relationships may start and end suddenly. With the square, restlessness can disrupt your plans just as they gain momentum. Integration comes from building flexible structures that allow both connection and freedom."
  },
  "uranus|mc": {
    theme: "Innovation meets vocation. Uranus brings originality, disruption and independence; the Midheaven is your career and public role. You negotiate how unconventional your path can be and how you handle change at work.",
    fusion: "Uranus conjunct the Midheaven often signals an unconventional career. You may work in technology, science, activism or other innovative fields, and you tend to resist rigid hierarchies. Career changes can be sudden, and you often become known for your originality. The shadow is instability, or difficulty staying with one role long enough to build authority.",
    flow: "You tend to find opportunities through innovation and change. Your originality supports your career, and you may be recognised as a forward thinker who sees what is coming. You adapt well to new trends. The ease can make you drift between interests without developing the expertise that would give your ideas real influence.",
    tension: "Career and freedom may clash. You might rebel against bosses, change jobs abruptly, or feel torn between security and independence. Home life may also feel disrupted by work upheavals. Integration involves creating a career with room for innovation, choosing change deliberately, and building a reputation sturdy enough to carry your originality."
  },
  "neptune|pluto": {
    theme: "Imagination meets transformation. Neptune dissolves and dreams; Pluto destroys and regenerates. This deeply generational pairing describes how collective ideals, spirituality and power evolve over long spans of history.",
    fusion: "Neptune conjunct Pluto last occurred in the early 1890s, so it rarely appears in living charts; most people born since the 1940s instead share a long sextile between them. Either way it is generational. It becomes personal only when it touches your Sun, Moon or angles. Then you may feel a strong pull towards spiritual transformation, depth psychology or collective healing.",
    flow: "The long sextile between Neptune and Pluto is shared by several generations and supports a gradual deepening of spiritual and psychological understanding. When it connects to your personal planets or angles, you tend to have a talent for sensing hidden currents in people and culture, and working with them creatively. The risk is taking this depth for granted and never putting it to use.",
    tension: "Neptune and Pluto have not formed a hard aspect within living memory, so in modern charts this is largely theoretical and entirely generational. If it does appear and touches your personal points, you may feel torn between ideals and power, or between surrender and control. Integration involves grounding spiritual longing in practical change, and noticing where collective fears shape your private choices."
  },
  "neptune|chiron": {
    theme: "Compassion meets the wound. Neptune brings empathy, imagination and longing; Chiron carries hurt and healing. You negotiate how sensitivity and spiritual openness can heal you instead of overwhelming you.",
    fusion: "Neptune conjunct Chiron often indicates a tender wound around boundaries, loss, addiction or spiritual disillusionment. You may absorb other people's pain easily, sometimes before you realise it is not yours. Over time you tend to develop real healing gifts through art, music, therapy or spiritual work. The challenge is protecting yourself while staying open to others.",
    flow: "You have a natural compassion and an intuitive feel for other people's pain. Healing, creative and spiritual work tend to suit you, and people often feel understood around you without needing to explain much. Music or water may be restorative for you. The ease can make you over-give, absorbing others' struggles and forgetting your own limits until you are depleted.",
    tension: "You may feel pulled between the wish to escape pain and the need to face it. This can show as avoidance, over-identifying with people who are suffering, or confusion about what your own wounds actually are. Relationships may involve rescuing. Integration involves clear boundaries, grounded self-care, and letting your sensitivity become a source of healing for yourself as well."
  },
  "neptune|northNode": {
    theme: "Dream meets direction. Neptune brings imagination, spirituality and longing; the North Node shows the growth your life keeps inviting. You negotiate whether your ideals guide your development or cloud it.",
    fusion: "Neptune on the North Node tends to make spiritual or creative growth part of your path. You may develop through art, compassion, service or intuition, and the most meaningful turns often come through surrender instead of planning. Direction can feel unclear for long stretches, and learning to trust becomes a lesson in itself. The challenge is to follow inspiration while taking practical steps.",
    flow: "Your intuition tends to support your growth. You often sense the right direction without knowing why, and creative or spiritual pursuits may open doors that effort alone could not. Synchronicities seem to guide you. The ease can make you passive, waiting for a sign when a simple, concrete action would move your life forward much faster.",
    tension: "Your ideals may conflict with your real development. You might follow illusions, idealise people who lead you off course, or avoid growth through escapism or self-sacrifice. Confusion about direction can be painful. Integration involves clarifying your goals, checking dreams against reality, and letting spirituality support your growth without standing in for it."
  },
  "neptune|lilith": {
    theme: "Dissolution meets the untamed. Neptune blurs, idealises and longs; Lilith holds raw, exiled instincts. You negotiate how to honour your hidden desires without losing yourself in fantasy or confusion.",
    fusion: "Neptune conjunct Lilith tends to give a mysterious, magnetic quality, especially around sexuality and the imagination. You may project your wild side into art, fantasy or spirituality. Others may see you as elusive. The risk is confusion about what you truly want, or being drawn into relationships where boundaries dissolve and you lose track of your own needs.",
    flow: "You have an intuitive, creative relationship with your shadow. You can express taboo or hidden feelings through art, dance, music or ritual, often beautifully and with real depth. Others may find you enchanting. The ease can make you avoid direct confrontation, letting your raw feelings stay in the realm of fantasy instead of being lived and spoken.",
    tension: "You may feel torn between idealised images of desire and your actual instincts. This can show as deception, self-deception, secret relationships or cycles of fascination and disillusionment. Shame may hide behind a fog of vagueness. Integration involves naming what you want clearly, setting honest boundaries, and using creative outlets to process what feels too big for words."
  },
  "neptune|asc": {
    theme: "Imagination meets presence. Neptune brings sensitivity, glamour and elusiveness; the Ascendant shapes how you appear and meet life. You negotiate how porous you are and how clearly others see you.",
    fusion: "Neptune conjunct the Ascendant tends to give a dreamy, receptive presence. People may project their ideals onto you, seeing what they wish to see. You are often sensitive to atmospheres, crowds and other people's moods, and you may be drawn to art, performance or healing. The shadow is losing yourself, or finding it hard to define and hold boundaries.",
    flow: "You come across as gentle, empathetic and creative. People tend to feel comfortable around you, and you adapt easily to different groups without much effort. Your imagination shows in how you dress or move. The ease can make you avoid clarity, letting others define you instead of stating plainly who you are and what you need.",
    tension: "Your sensitivity may make it hard to hold a clear sense of self. With the opposition, you may idealise partners, or attract people who need rescuing. With the square, you might feel confused about how you come across. Integration involves grounding practices, clear boundaries, and letting your compassion flow from a stable centre."
  },
  "neptune|mc": {
    theme: "Dream meets vocation. Neptune brings inspiration, idealism and fluidity; the Midheaven is your career and public role. You negotiate how to turn a vision into work without losing direction or credibility.",
    fusion: "Neptune conjunct the Midheaven often signals a vocation connected to art, film, music, healing, spirituality or service. You may be seen as inspiring, glamorous or hard to pin down. Career direction can feel unclear for long periods, and your path often unfolds through intuition. The risk is instability, or unclear expectations in the workplace that leave you undervalued.",
    flow: "Your career tends to benefit from imagination and compassion. You may find meaningful work through creative or caring fields, and people often respond to your vision. Opportunities can arrive through intuition or chance meetings. The ease can make you drift, trusting that things will work out without the concrete steps that would build a lasting reputation.",
    tension: "Career and ideals may feel mismatched. You might feel confused about your direction, idealise jobs or bosses, or experience disappointment in public life. Home and career may blur together. Integration involves grounding your vocation in clear goals, checking facts and contracts carefully, and allowing your ideals to shape your work without losing touch with practical needs."
  },
  "pluto|chiron": {
    theme: "Power meets the wound. Pluto brings intensity, depth and transformation; Chiron carries hurt and healing. You negotiate how deep pain can become the source of profound strength instead of a lifelong weight.",
    fusion: "Pluto conjunct Chiron is partly generational, shared by those born during certain years in the 1940s and 1990s, and it reflects collective wounds around power and survival. When it touches your personal planets or angles, it can indicate intense experiences of loss or crisis. Over time you tend to develop deep healing insight, often working with trauma, grief or transformation.",
    flow: "You tend to have a natural capacity for regeneration. You can move through painful experiences and emerge wiser, and others may seek you out in their own crises. Psychology, crisis work and deep therapy may suit you. The ease can make you minimise your own need for support, assuming you can always handle it alone.",
    tension: "You may feel caught between pain and the fear of losing control. This can show as defensiveness, obsession with old hurts, or intense relationships that repeat old wounds. Integration involves allowing yourself to be vulnerable, seeking skilled support, and using your hard-won insight to help others heal without taking on their burdens."
  },
  "pluto|northNode": {
    theme: "Transformation meets direction. Pluto brings depth, intensity and change; the North Node shows the growth your life keeps inviting. You negotiate how profound change supports your development and how to handle power.",
    fusion: "Pluto on the North Node tends to make transformation central to your path. You may grow through crisis, loss or deep psychological work, and life may repeatedly ask you to let go of the old. Power can be a major theme. The challenge is to use intensity wisely, allowing each ending to open a new chapter.",
    flow: "Your capacity for change tends to support your growth. You often recognise when something must end, and you can reinvent yourself in powerful ways. Others may sense your depth and turn to you for guidance. The ease can make you over-rely on intensity, seeking dramatic change when steadier progress would serve you better.",
    tension: "Deep change may seem to pull you away from your growth. You might resist necessary endings, or become caught in power struggles that distract from your real direction. Fear of loss can keep you stuck. Integration involves accepting transformation, choosing to let go consciously, and using your strength to move towards meaningful growth."
  },
  "pluto|lilith": {
    theme: "Power meets the untamed. Pluto brings depth, intensity and control; Lilith holds raw, exiled instincts. You negotiate how to own your hidden power and desire without being ruled by them.",
    fusion: "Pluto conjunct Lilith gives a potent, magnetic intensity, especially around sexuality, anger and power. You may have experienced early control or taboo around your instincts. Over time this tends to become a fierce authenticity, a refusal to be diminished. The risk is using that power to dominate or to punish those who remind you of old wounds.",
    flow: "You have an easy relationship with depth and intensity. You tend to accept your instincts fully and can help others face their own shadows without fear. Psychology, sexuality and transformative work may suit you. The ease can make you careless with the power you hold, forgetting how overwhelming your intensity can feel to others.",
    tension: "You may feel caught between the fear of your own power and the urge to unleash it. This can show as control dynamics, jealousy or cycles of suppression and eruption. Relationships may feel intense and consuming. Integration involves owning your desires openly, using your power responsibly, and allowing vulnerability to soften your defences."
  },
  "pluto|asc": {
    theme: "Power meets presence. Pluto brings intensity, depth and control; the Ascendant shapes how you appear and meet life. You negotiate how much of your inner force others see, and how you handle influence.",
    fusion: "Pluto conjunct the Ascendant tends to give an intense, magnetic presence. People may find you powerful, private or hard to read. You often approach life strategically and prefer to reveal yourself slowly. Your life may involve several major reinventions. The shadow is secrecy, control or a defensive stance that keeps people from getting close.",
    flow: "You come across as capable and quietly powerful. People tend to trust you in a crisis, and you have a natural ability to read what is going on beneath the surface. You can reinvent yourself when needed. The ease can make you rely on control, or overlook how much impact your presence has on others.",
    tension: "Power dynamics may be a recurring theme. With the opposition, you may attract intense partners, or feel that relationships transform you whether you like it or not. With the square, you might feel pressure to control how you are seen. Integration involves letting others in, using your strength openly, and allowing relationships to be places of shared power."
  },
  "pluto|mc": {
    theme: "Power meets vocation. Pluto brings intensity, ambition and transformation; the Midheaven is your career and public role. You negotiate how to use influence responsibly and how much change your career can hold.",
    fusion: "Pluto conjunct the Midheaven often signals a powerful career drive. You may be drawn to work involving research, psychology, finance, medicine or crisis management, and you tend to seek real influence. Your career may involve major transformations. The shadow is power struggles with authority, or an all-or-nothing approach to success.",
    flow: "Your career tends to benefit from depth and strategic insight. You can see what needs to change in an organisation or field, and others often respect your quiet authority, especially when things go wrong. You work well behind the scenes. The ease can make you comfortable with your influence and less aware of how strongly it affects colleagues.",
    tension: "Career and power may clash. You might struggle with controlling bosses, or feel compelled to prove yourself relentlessly. Home and family dynamics may also influence your ambitions. Integration involves choosing work that matters to you, using your influence ethically, and allowing your career to evolve through natural endings and new beginnings."
  },
  "chiron|asc": {
    theme: "The wound meets presence. Chiron carries hurt and healing; the Ascendant shapes how you appear and approach life. You negotiate how visible your sensitivity is and how your story shapes first impressions.",
    fusion: "Chiron conjunct the Ascendant often indicates a wound connected to identity, appearance or the body. You may have felt different or exposed early on. Over time this tends to give you a remarkable ability to make others feel accepted. People may sense your vulnerability and trust you. The challenge is not letting old hurt define how you present yourself.",
    flow: "You come across as approachable and empathetic. People often feel safe telling you their struggles, sometimes within minutes of meeting you, and you have a natural gift for putting others at ease. Healing, teaching or coaching may suit you. The ease can make you focus on other people's wounds and quietly neglect your own care.",
    tension: "You may feel self-conscious about how you are seen, or attract partners who touch old wounds. With the square, insecurity can show as overcompensation or withdrawal. Integration involves accepting your vulnerability, allowing others to see the real you, and letting your story become a source of compassion and strength."
  },
  "chiron|mc": {
    theme: "The wound meets vocation. Chiron carries hurt and healing; the Midheaven is your career and public role. You negotiate how your personal pain can shape a meaningful professional path.",
    fusion: "Chiron conjunct the Midheaven often signals a vocation connected to healing, teaching or mentoring. You may have experienced a wound around career, recognition or parental expectations. Over time this tends to become a calling, and you may be known for helping others through difficulty. The challenge is feeling confident in your authority despite old doubts.",
    flow: "Your career tends to benefit from empathy and lived experience. You may find meaningful work in healing, counselling or education, and others respect your honesty about struggle. Colleagues often bring you their problems. The ease can make you undervalue your skills, charge too little, or give so much of yourself at work that little is left for home.",
    tension: "Career and personal wounds may seem intertwined. You might feel unworthy of success, or experience setbacks that reopen old hurts. Home and work may compete. Integration involves recognising that your wounds give you unique insight, and building a career that honours both your gifts and your limits."
  },
  "northNode|asc": {
    theme: "Direction meets presence. The North Node shows the growth your life invites; the Ascendant shapes how you appear and approach the world. You negotiate how your identity supports your development.",
    fusion: "The North Node conjunct the Ascendant tends to make personal growth highly visible. You may develop by becoming more independent, self-aware and assertive, and life often invites you to step into your own identity. This can feel uncomfortable at first. The challenge is to balance growth in self-expression with care for relationships.",
    flow: "Your personality tends to support your growth. When you act authentically and put yourself forward, opportunities appear, and people respond warmly to the person you are becoming. First impressions often work in your favour. The ease can make you overlook the areas that still need attention, assuming growth will happen automatically simply because your manner opens doors.",
    tension: "How you present yourself may pull against your growth. You might hide behind a persona, or rely on others to define you. With the South Node on the Ascendant, the North Node sits on the Descendant, pointing growth towards partnership. Integration involves learning to balance self and other, and allowing relationships to help you grow."
  },
  "northNode|mc": {
    theme: "Direction meets vocation. The North Node shows your path of growth; the Midheaven is your career and public role. You negotiate how your work and ambitions connect with your development.",
    fusion: "The North Node conjunct the Midheaven tends to make career a key area of growth. You may develop through ambition, public responsibility or building a reputation. Life often invites you to step into visible roles. The challenge is balancing that growth with the needs of home and family, which may feel more comfortable.",
    flow: "Your career tends to support your growth. When you pursue meaningful work, opportunities appear, and people in positions of influence recognise your potential and open doors. Public responsibility suits you more than you might expect. The ease can make you comfortable in a role that no longer stretches you, long after the real learning has finished.",
    tension: "Your career and your growth may pull in different directions. You might feel torn between public ambition and private needs, or struggle to find work that matches your path. Integration involves choosing a direction that honours both, and letting your development guide your professional choices."
  },
  "lilith|asc": {
    theme: "The untamed meets presence. Lilith holds raw, exiled instincts; the Ascendant shapes how you appear and meet life. You negotiate how much of your wildness shows and how others respond to it.",
    fusion: "Lilith conjunct the Ascendant tends to give a striking, magnetic presence. People may see you as unconventional, provocative or intensely independent. You may have been judged for being too much. Over time this can become powerful authenticity. The risk is defensiveness, or expecting rejection before it happens.",
    flow: "You come across as confident in your difference. People tend to find your honesty refreshing, and you may inspire others to drop their masks and be more authentic. You rarely pretend to be someone you are not. The ease can make you careless with how your intensity lands, especially with gentler people who need more time to trust you.",
    tension: "Your raw instincts may clash with how you want to be seen. With the opposition, partners may seem to carry the wildness you hide. With the square, you might swing between conformity and rebellion. Integration involves owning your whole self, and letting your authenticity become a source of strength in relationships."
  },
  "lilith|mc": {
    theme: "The untamed meets vocation. Lilith holds raw, exiled instincts; the Midheaven is your career and public role. You negotiate how your independence and difference show up in your work and reputation.",
    fusion: "Lilith conjunct the Midheaven often signals an unconventional or controversial career path. You may challenge norms in your field, or be known for your independence. Authority figures may have tried to restrict you. Over time this can become a powerful public voice. The risk is conflict with institutions.",
    flow: "Your career tends to benefit from originality and courage. You can speak up for the marginalised or challenge outdated practices in your field, and people tend to respect your honesty even when it unsettles them. The ease can make you underestimate the patience and political skill needed to turn a bold stance into lasting change.",
    tension: "Career and authenticity may seem at odds. You might feel pressured to hide parts of yourself to succeed, or clash with authority. Home and public life may compete. Integration involves building a career that allows you to be fully yourself, and choosing your battles strategically."
  }
};
